  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(109, 103, 101);">Remark.</html:span> The int8 column only doubles from v5p onward — v3 and v4p run int8 through the <fr:link href="/OGCRP/" title="Matrix Multiply Unit (MXU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/OGCRP/" display-uri="OGCRP" type="local">MXU</fr:link> at the same rate as bf16, so quantizing there saves memory traffic but buys no extra OPs/s. The ratio of a FLOPs/s column to the HBM bandwidth column is the <fr:link href="/scaling-ch1/" title="Scaling Book: Exercises › All about rooflines" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/scaling-ch1/" display-uri="scaling-ch1" type="local">roofline</fr:link> ridge point: on v5e, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[3.94e14 / 8.2e11 \approx  480]]></fr:tex>, i.e. batch <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[240]]></fr:tex> in the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[2B]]></fr:tex> arithmetic-intensity approximation.</html:div>
<html:p>Interconnect bandwidth is quoted per <html:em>link</html:em>, not per chip — multiply by the number of neighbors a chip has in the topology above to get its aggregate off-chip bandwidth.</html:p>
